                        "entry_id": "eed6b94a-a56f-384a-b9aa-c4f5334eb185",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An advocate of constructionism."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8dd63a66-5bcd-4a3c-8eb8-b4b0a9f28f70",
                                "sense_id": "234c16d4-8b6a-31d4-afaf-c3f9fc7e31b3",
                                "text": "Aristotle claimed that people were by nature political animals, thus inaugurating the essentialist argument for the state. The constructionists similarly believe that the modern state is an overriding necessity, a built-in impulse that cannot be resisted any more than the St. Laurence River making its way to the sea."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "222586e9-e3e3-332f-bba9-19d11b0c5bd8",
                        "entry_id": "eed6b94a-a56f-384a-b9aa-c4f5334eb185",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who puts a certain construction upon some writing or instrument, such as the United States Constitution."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "49497671-58f7-4ef6-856b-50897ee60e26",
                                "sense_id": "222586e9-e3e3-332f-bba9-19d11b0c5bd8",
                                "text": "a strict constructionist; a broad constructionist"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "950b76be-4a04-38d0-9ae8-4aab683a1ef7",
                        "entry_id": "eed6b94a-a56f-384a-b9aa-c4f5334eb185",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who works in construction."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "98ef7034-d050-489c-955d-1d667658a79f",
                                "sense_id": "950b76be-4a04-38d0-9ae8-4aab683a1ef7",
                                "text": "The gap that remains in the interior will no doubt be eventually bridged over by railway communication; and thus the great continent will no longer be a terra incognita to the general world, who have hitherto only heard of the splendid country through which the railway will pass, from the reports of telegraph constructionists and overlanding parties."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
